<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ashdown</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">871</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ashdown was fought on 8 January 871 between the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a>, led by King Æthelred I and his brother Alfred, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-heathen-army">Great Heathen Army</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a>. Alfred's attack uphill began a West Saxon victory in which the Danish king Bagsecg and five earls were killed. The site, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berkshire">Berkshire</a> Downs, is not known exactly, and the Danes won further victories later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ashdown.jpg" alt="Battle of Ashdown" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Doyle (died 1883) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Ashdown.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
